.TH JJMCP 1 "May 2026" "JJMCP 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jjmcp \- local MCP server for a tmux Julia REPL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jjmcp
.B --help
.br
.B jjmcp
.B serve
.RB [ \-\-transcript
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-transcript\-format
.IR text | jsonl ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B JohnJuliaMCP
(
.B JJMCP
) is a local JSON-RPC 2.0 MCP server that lets MCP clients work through an existing tmux pane running Julia.
The tmux Julia REPL is treated as the source of truth.
JJMCP does not start hidden Julia workers by default.
.PP
In
.B serve
mode, stdout is reserved for MCP protocol frames.
Diagnostics are written to stderr.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B --help
Print usage to stdout and exit.
.TP
.B serve
Run MCP over stdio.
.TP
.BI \-\-transcript " path"
Append every tool call and its result to
.I path
(see TRANSCRIPT).
Overrides
.B JJMCP_TRANSCRIPT.
.TP
.BI \-\-transcript\-format " text|jsonl"
Transcript format, default text.
Overrides
.B JJMCP_TRANSCRIPT_FORMAT.
.SH MCP TOOLS
.TP
.B jjmcp_list_tmux
List tmux sessions, windows, panes, pane ids, active process names, titles, and current paths.
.TP
.B jjmcp_bind
Bind to an existing tmux pane.
Arguments:
.B target
and optional
.B project_root.
.TP
.B jjmcp_status
Report the current binding, pane information, marker state, timestamp, and liveness.
.TP
.B jjmcp_eval
Evaluate Julia code in the bound pane.
Arguments:
.B code,
optional
.B timeout_ms,
and optional
.B capture_lines.
When using the tmux transport, eval-style tools are pasted as
.B @JJMCP_COMMAND
macro calls after a one-time runtime bootstrap in the Julia REPL.
.TP
.B jjmcp_capture
Capture recent pane output without sending input.
.TP
.B jjmcp_capture_test_results
Capture pane output and parse the latest Julia `Test Summary:` block, returning pass/fail/total counts
and a compact failures list.
.TP
.B jjmcp_interrupt
Send Ctrl-C to the bound pane.
.TP
.B jjmcp_revise
Run
.B Revise.revise()
in the bound pane.
.TP
.B jjmcp_activate
Run
.B using Pkg; Pkg.activate(path)
in the bound pane.
.TP
.B jjmcp_test
Run focused Julia tests in the existing REPL context.
.TP
.B jjmcp_transcript
Start the transcript
.RB ( path ,
optional
.BR format ),
stop it
.RB ( enabled
false), or report it (no arguments).
.SH TRANSCRIPT
The transcript records every tool call: its time, tool and bound pane, the Julia code JJMCP sent or the
tool's arguments, and the result before the MCP size limits (up to 8 MiB per call, keeping the end).
Entries are appended; the file can be read, truncated, or rotated while the server runs.
Relative paths are taken from the server's working directory.
.B jjmcp_status
shows the current file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B JJMCP_TIMEOUT_MS_MAX
Upper bound on tool
.B timeout_ms
(default 600000).
.TP
.B JJMCP_LOG_FORMAT
.B json
for one JSON object per stderr log line (default text).
.TP
.B JJMCP_TRANSCRIPT
Transcript file, as
.B \-\-transcript.
.TP
.B JJMCP_TRANSCRIPT_FORMAT
.B text
(default) or
.B jsonl.
.SH LONG RUNS
Eval-style tools accept
.B timeout_ms.
The default per-process maximum is 600000 ms.
Set
.B JJMCP_TIMEOUT_MS_MAX
before starting
.B jjmcp serve
to allow longer calls.
.PP
When eval output is larger than the MCP response budget, JJMCP returns the end of the captured output
and includes a truncation marker for omitted earlier lines or bytes.
The full output remains visible in the bound tmux pane scrollback, and in the transcript when one is enabled.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
tmux new-session -s julia
julia --project=.

build/jjmcp serve
.fi
.PP
From an MCP client, call
.B jjmcp_list_tmux,
then bind to the desired pane id with
.B jjmcp_bind.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .jjmcp/config.json
Optional local binding persistence file.
.TP
.I ~/.jjmcp/settings.json
Transcript settings
.RB ( transcript ,
.BR transcript_format ),
used when neither
.B \-\-transcript
nor
.B JJMCP_TRANSCRIPT
gives a transcript.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jjmcp-config (5),
.BR jjmcp-security (7),
.BR tmux (1),
.BR julia (1)
